  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03VV">Remark <span data-tag="03VV">64.31.4</span>.</a> We now have, thanks to Lafforgue and many other mathematicians, complete theorems like this two above for $\text{GL}_ n$ and allowing ramification! In other words, the full global Langlands correspondence for $\text{GL}_ n$ is known for function fields of curves over finite fields. At the same time this does not mean there aren't a lot of interesting questions left to answer about the fundamental groups of curves over finite fields, as we shall see below. </p>
